smithy dev turns your coding agent into a small engineering team. The skills
call it for evidence, waits and batches; you run it to set up, check and watch
the work. Two builds: the skills build (this one) and the harness build; the
harness build adds the daemon, chat, web UI and board.

Start here
  doctor        check everything a warden batch needs (--quiet: problems only;
                --fix [--yes]: apply fixes)
  setup         use-smithy setup: installed skills, settings, instructions block
  status        every task list and batch on this machine
  version       print the version
  welcome       the first-run walk again: agents, model, API keys, notifications
                (harness build)

Daily
  attach        watch a daemon live: events, decisions, reconnect and resume
                (harness build)
  auto          autonomous intake: poll issue sources, take queued issues,
                report back, serve the loop
  board         built-in tracker: add, list, show, set, claim, sync (harness
                build)
  chat          fullscreen chat over a daemon (also bare smithy, which starts
                the daemon) (harness build)
  daemon        run the auto loop with a local API (events, decisions) (harness
                build)
  pair          one-time code another machine trades for a device token (harness
                build)
  receipt       run a command and record it as evidence for a claim
  report        weekly report: shipped, failed, time and cost per harness, open
                decisions
  scan          check a change's added lines and files for secrets
  schedule      start workflows on a cron, webhook, GitHub event or file change
                (harness build)
  search        search ADRs, glossary and docs, best sources first (--code: the
                whole repo)
  servers       the daemons this machine talks to: list, add, use, discover
                (harness build)
  stats         live stats of the forge: agents, incoming issues, what needs
                you, activity
  stop          stop the local background daemon (harness build)
  tasks         the shared task list (smithy tasks board --all)
  wait          wait without tokens for PRs, runs, branches, issues or a batch
  web           print or open the daemon's web UI link (harness build)
  workflow      workflows: flows of steps you run: list, show, run, history,
                validate (harness build)

Accounts and secrets
  auth          source API keys in ~/.smithy/auth.json: set (stdin only), list,
                remove, bind, ask
  config        settings and models (smithy config list)
  notify        Telegram notifications from smithy auto serve: test, status
  pool          your own agent accounts for smithy agent: add, login, list,
                remove, clear

Maintenance
  bench         run smithy's benchmark task set with an agent
  cleanup       remove a finished task's worktree and local branch, or old
                builds, images and worktrees
  skills        find installed skills (smithy skills --list)
  uninstall     remove smithy: binaries, the skills it installed, daemon,
                images, PATH line (lists first)
  update        update the binary and the skills to the latest release

Used by the skills
  adr           next numbered ADR (smithy adr "<title>" [adr-dir])
  agent         run one headless agent CLI on a prompt file
  batch         write, set or extend a warden batch.json (init, set, add)
  brief         render a warden worker's brief from batch.json
  cards         warden status cards
  changed       source files changed against a base (--csv for Stryker)
  comments      check the comment policy (smithy comments [paths] | --diff
                <base>)
  commit        atomic commits in the repo's message style
  consult       ask the strongest model to settle one decision
  decide        optional decision model: rule flags and question impact
  decisions     the log of the user's decisions taken without them
  drift         doc-drift report against a base (smithy drift [base])
  guard         dangerous-command guard: check a command, Claude Code hook, list
                the rules
  guard-tests   pre-edit hook: blocks test edits in the green phase
  harness       "<harness> <adapter>" for this shell
  mcp           MCP server (stdio) for driven CLIs: board, ask, secret calls,
                search (harness build)
  names         branch and worktree names
  pr            pull requests that follow the repo's PR template
  pr-state      compact JSON state of one PR (tend)
  proxy         egress proxy with bound secrets, run natively: serve, approve,
                deny
  route         pick the model tier for a task
  stack         the repo's test tooling as key: value lines
  task-dir      resolve and create the task dir for a plan slug
  verify        proof for a worker's PR claim
  wait-turn     a launched warden worker waits for its prereqs and a free slot
  worktree      create a task worktree at its standard path

(harness build): the release binary; install it with smithy update, or go build
-tags harness ./cmd/smithy.
Run smithy help <command> for usage and examples. Not on PATH? smithy setup
path.
Exit codes: 0 success, 1 failure, 2 usage error (3 where a command's help says).
